IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccsa-services`

-- Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) -- the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters (the Q&A
-- layer).
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The baseline (ccsa-services.l4) was written from the seat of the parent using child care (s 3 "parent"). That
-- is the first role. The second is the person who provides, or plans to provide, the service: the Act's duties fall on
-- them (s 9, the licence; s 18, the supervising officer's presence as a licence condition; s 20, the licence's terms;
-- s 36, advertising; s 29(4)(b)(ii), a refund order; s 25, suspension). The CEO, the Minister and the State
-- Administrative Tribunal are never a seat: what they may or must do appears only as what it means for the person. The
-- supervising officer is not a seat either: s 18 puts the duty of their presence on the licensee.
--
-- SITUATIONS (graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's fact
-- straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not hold, without reading anything else.
-- The questions of one situation share ONE input, the same name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once:
--   - `the CEO has suspended the service's licence by notice` (parent, provider): the 60-day cap on the suspension
--     (s 25(3)(b)) and the 21 days within which the CEO must go to the Tribunal (s 25(4)).
-- Every other question arises in every situation of its role, so takes no situation input. Which law governs the service
-- (the National Law or this Act) is not a situation: it is the baseline's own first question, worked out from the
-- Service record, and every later question already answers "not for this Act" where the National Law governs.
--
-- The rules are the baseline's. This module calls the baseline's functions and restates none. The provider's own
-- questions on the s 36 fine, a refund order and publication (s 45A) are helpers here. Every answer type carries
-- `does not arise for you`. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- THE FIVE s 29(2) GROUNDS ARE ASKED AS ONE (fixed 6 November 2026, after verification). The baseline reads them only as
-- "any of (a) to (e)", so the two refund questions ask `a ground for disciplinary action in s 29(2) exists` and pass it
-- to the baseline as ground (a), the others FALSE: the same answer for every input. Asked as five, with the Service
-- record (448 combinations), they made 14 336 combinations, past the 1 024 the site's form tries before it gives up
-- dropping a question for the other role; now 896.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may`
    `I provide the service, or plan to`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    months HAS `number of months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    days HAS `number of days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Governing law answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `governed by` HAS `the governing law` IS A `The law that governs it`

DECLARE `Licence answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the licence needed` HAS `what it needs` IS A `What licence it needs`

DECLARE `Lawfulness answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `lawful or not` HAS `the lawfulness` IS A `Is it lawful`

DECLARE `Fee refund answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `refund` HAS `the refund` IS A `Fee refund`

-- The provider's side of s 29(4)(b)(ii), (5), worded from the provider's seat. Not in the baseline.
DECLARE `Refund order answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `possible: the Tribunal may order you to refund fees to the parents or others who paid them, if the CEO alleges and the Tribunal is satisfied grounds exist, even after you stop being a licensee (s 29(4)(b)(ii), (5))`
    `no: no ground for disciplinary action is stated (s 29(2))`
    `not under this Act: it does not license the service`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The baseline's refund answer, read from the provider's seat. Every value is listed, with no OTHERWISE.
GIVEN `the refund` IS A `Fee refund`
GIVETH A `Refund order answer`
`the provider's side of` `the refund` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the refund`
    WHEN `possible: the Tribunal may order the licensee to refund my fees, if the CEO alleges and the Tribunal is satisfied grounds exist` THEN `possible: the Tribunal may order you to refund fees to the parents or others who paid them, if the CEO alleges and the Tribunal is satisfied grounds exist, even after you stop being a licensee (s 29(4)(b)(ii), (5))`
    WHEN `no: no ground for disciplinary action is stated` THEN `no: no ground for disciplinary action is stated (s 29(2))`
    WHEN `not under this Act: it does not license the service` THEN `not under this Act: it does not license the service`

-- s 36 Penalty: "a fine of $6 000". s 45A(3): published information "may identify a particular child care service or a
-- particular person, but not a child"; (4) only if the CEO is "satisfied that it is in the public interest".
`s 36 -- the fine for advertising without a licence or exemption` MEANS 6000

GIVEN `the CEO is satisfied it is in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 45A(1), (3), (4) -- the CEO may publish information identifying the service or the provider` IF
    `the CEO is satisfied it is in the public interest`

§§ `For the parent, and for the provider`

§§§ `ss 4, 5B, 9, 45 -- which law governs the service, and must it be licensed`

@export Is this service a "child care service" under the Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) (s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the service` IS A Service @desc The service: whether it gives education and care on a regular basis to children under 13, who gives the care, which National Law exclusion (if any) it falls in, whether the Child Care Services regulations prescribe its type, and whether an approved provider runs it where an approved education and care service is run
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this service a child care service under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN `yes if` (`Is it a child care service under this Act` `the service`)
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN `yes if` (`Is it a child care service under this Act` `the service`)

@export Which law governs this service: the Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA), or the Education and Care Services National Law (WA) (s 4, s 5B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the service` IS A Service @desc The service: whether it gives education and care on a regular basis to children under 13, who gives the care, which National Law exclusion (if any) it falls in, whether the Child Care Services regulations prescribe its type, and whether an approved provider runs it where an approved education and care service is run
GIVETH A `Governing law answer`
`Which law governs this service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN `governed by` (`Which law governs the service my child attends` `the service`)
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN `governed by` (`Which law governs the service my child attends` `the service`)

@export Must this service hold a licence under the Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) (s 9, s 45, s 5B(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the service` IS A Service @desc The service: whether it gives education and care on a regular basis to children under 13, who gives the care, which National Law exclusion (if any) it falls in, whether the Child Care Services regulations prescribe its type, and whether an approved provider runs it where an approved education and care service is run
      `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial order published in the Gazette under s 45(1)(a) exempts this service, or its type, from s 9
GIVETH A `Licence answer`
`Must this service hold a licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN `the licence needed` (`Must the service hold a licence` `the service` `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order`)
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN `the licence needed` (`Must the service hold a licence` `the service` `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order`)

@export Is this service being provided lawfully under the Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) (ss 9, 13, 20, 21, 22(3), 45(3B))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the service` IS A Service @desc The service: whether it gives education and care on a regular basis to children under 13, who gives the care, which National Law exclusion (if any) it falls in, whether the Child Care Services regulations prescribe its type, and whether an approved provider runs it where an approved education and care service is run
      `the status` IS A `Licence status` @desc The state of the service's licence (for an associated children's service, its National Law service approval): in effect, ended with a renewal lodged in time and undecided, ended with no renewal, suspended, cancelled, surrendered, or none held
      `the licence is for this type of service at this place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licence names this type of service and this place (s 13(1))
      `it is run in accordance with the licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is being run in accordance with its licence and its conditions
      `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial order published in the Gazette under s 45(1)(a) exempts this service, or its type, from s 9
      `it complies with the exemption's conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service complies with any conditions in that order (s 45(3B))
GIVETH A `Lawfulness answer`
`Is this service being provided lawfully` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN `lawful or not` (`Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `the service` `the status` `the licence is for this type of service at this place` `it is run in accordance with the licence` `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order` `it complies with the exemption's conditions`)
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN `lawful or not` (`Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `the service` `the status` `the licence is for this type of service at this place` `it is run in accordance with the licence` `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order` `it complies with the exemption's conditions`)

§§§ `s 9 penalty -- providing a child care service without a licence`

@export What is the most the provider can be fined for providing a child care service without a licence, in dollars (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is a first offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this would be the provider's first s 9 offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the provider can be fined for providing it unlicensed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN amount (`What is the most the provider can be fined for running unlicensed` `it is a first offence`)
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN amount (`What is the most the provider can be fined for running unlicensed` `it is a first offence`)

@export What daily penalty does the provider face for each day a child care service runs without a licence, in dollars (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is a first offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this would be the provider's first s 9 offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What daily penalty does the provider face for each day unlicensed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN amount (`What is the daily penalty for running unlicensed` `it is a first offence`)
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN amount (`What is the daily penalty for running unlicensed` `it is a first offence`)

@export What is the longest the provider can be imprisoned for providing a child care service without a licence, in months (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is a first offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this would be the provider's first s 9 offence
GIVETH A `Months`
`What is the longest the provider can be imprisoned for providing it unlicensed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN months (`What is the longest the provider can be imprisoned for running unlicensed` `it is a first offence`)
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN months (`What is the longest the provider can be imprisoned for running unlicensed` `it is a first offence`)

§§§ `ss 18, 36 -- the supervising officer, and advertising`

@export Must the supervising officer be present while the service is caring for the children (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 18)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the service` IS A Service @desc The service: whether it gives education and care on a regular basis to children under 13, who gives the care, which National Law exclusion (if any) it falls in, whether the Child Care Services regulations prescribe its type, and whether an approved provider runs it where an approved education and care service is run
      `the regulations provide otherwise for this time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations relieve the licensee of the s 18 condition at this time (regulations not deposited)
      `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial order published in the Gazette under s 45(1)(a) exempts this service, or its type, from s 9
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the supervising officer be there while the service runs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN `yes if` (`Must the supervising officer be present` `the service` `the regulations provide otherwise for this time` `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order`)
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN `yes if` (`Must the supervising officer be present` `the service` `the regulations provide otherwise for this time` `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order`)

@export May the provider advertise, or hold out, that it provides the child care service (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 36)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it holds a licence authorising the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider holds a licence authorising the service it advertises
      `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial order published in the Gazette under s 45(1)(a) exempts this service, or its type, from s 9
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the provider advertise the child care service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN `yes if` (`May the provider advertise the service` `it holds a licence authorising the service` `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order`)
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN `yes if` (`May the provider advertise the service` `it holds a licence authorising the service` `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order`)

§§§ `s 25 -- suspension of the licence by notice`

-- Situation: the CEO has given the licensee written notice suspending the licence (s 25(1)).
@export For how many days at most can a suspension of the service's licence by the CEO's notice last (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 25(3)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the CEO has suspended the service's licence by notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has given the licensee written notice suspending the service's licence, on reasonable grounds of an unacceptable risk to the children's wellbeing (s 25(1))
GIVETH A `Days`
`For how many days at most can the suspension last` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN
        IF `the CEO has suspended the service's licence by notice`
        THEN days `What is the longest the CEO can suspend the licence in days`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN
        IF `the CEO has suspended the service's licence by notice`
        THEN days `What is the longest the CEO can suspend the licence in days`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many days of the suspension notice must the CEO take the matter to the State Administrative Tribunal, unless the suspension is revoked (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 25(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the CEO has suspended the service's licence by notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has given the licensee written notice suspending the service's licence, on reasonable grounds of an unacceptable risk to the children's wellbeing (s 25(1))
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days must the CEO take the suspension to the Tribunal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN
        IF `the CEO has suspended the service's licence by notice`
        THEN days `Within how many days must the CEO go to the Tribunal`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN
        IF `the CEO has suspended the service's licence by notice`
        THEN days `Within how many days must the CEO go to the Tribunal`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the parent`

§§§ `ss 29, 45A -- my fees, and my child's privacy`

@export Could the provider of my child's service be ordered to refund my fees (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 29(4)(b)(ii))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the service` IS A Service @desc The service: whether it gives education and care on a regular basis to children under 13, who gives the care, which National Law exclusion (if any) it falls in, whether the Child Care Services regulations prescribe its type, and whether an approved provider runs it where an approved education and care service is run
      `a ground for disciplinary action in s 29(2) exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of these holds: the licensee improperly obtained its licence (s 29(2)(a)); contravened the Child Care Services Act 2007 (b); the CEO is no longer satisfied as to a matter in s 14(3), 15(2) or 16(2) that was relevant to granting the licence (c); the licensee contravened the Working with Children (Screening) Act 2004 s 22 (d); or there are reasonable grounds for believing that continuing the service would be an unacceptable risk to the children's wellbeing (e)
GIVETH A `Fee refund answer`
`Could I get my child care fees refunded` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN `refund` (`Could I be refunded my fees` `the service` `a ground for disciplinary action in s 29(2) exists` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the CEO publish information about child care services that identifies my child (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 45A(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the CEO publish information that identifies my child` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may` THEN `yes if` `May the CEO publish information identifying my child`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the provider`

§§§ `ss 29, 36, 45A -- a refund order, the advertising fine, and publication`

@export Could I be ordered to refund fees to the parents or others who paid them (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 29(2), (4)(b)(ii), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the service` IS A Service @desc The service: whether it gives education and care on a regular basis to children under 13, who gives the care, which National Law exclusion (if any) it falls in, whether the Child Care Services regulations prescribe its type, and whether an approved provider runs it where an approved education and care service is run
      `a ground for disciplinary action in s 29(2) exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of these holds: the licensee improperly obtained its licence (s 29(2)(a)); contravened the Child Care Services Act 2007 (b); the CEO is no longer satisfied as to a matter in s 14(3), 15(2) or 16(2) that was relevant to granting the licence (c); the licensee contravened the Working with Children (Screening) Act 2004 s 22 (d); or there are reasonable grounds for believing that continuing the service would be an unacceptable risk to the children's wellbeing (e)
GIVETH A `Refund order answer`
`Could I be ordered to refund fees` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN `the provider's side of` (`Could I be refunded my fees` `the service` `a ground for disciplinary action in s 29(2) exists` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for advertising, or holding out, that I provide a child care service without a licence or exemption (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 36)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for advertising without a licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN amount `s 36 -- the fine for advertising without a licence or exemption`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the CEO publish information that identifies me or my service, such as compliance notices and Tribunal orders (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 45A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the CEO is satisfied it is in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO is satisfied that publishing the information is in the public interest (the CEO's judgment, s 45A(4))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the CEO publish information that identifies me or my service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I provide the service, or plan to` THEN `yes if` (`s 45A(1), (3), (4) -- the CEO may publish information identifying the service or the provider` `the CEO is satisfied it is in the public interest`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
